Shipped inside the games Diorama builds (assets/web), each with its licence beside it:
- three.js r172 and its GLTFLoader, https://threejs.org, MIT (lib/three/LICENSE). Copyright (c) the three.js authors.
- jsartoolkit5, https://github.com/artoolkitx/jsartoolkit5, LGPL-3.0 (lib/LICENSE-jsartoolkit5.txt), in Markers games.
  Copyright (c) the ARToolKit and artoolkitX authors.
- MindAR 1.2.5 and three.js 0.160, https://github.com/hiukim/mind-ar-js, MIT (lib/mindar), in Images and Faces games.
- OpenCV.js 4.10 (the @techstark/opencv-js build), https://opencv.org, Apache License 2.0 (lib/opencv/LICENSE),
  in Surfaces games: the surface tracker for cameras without ARCore.
- JoltPhysics.js 1.1.1 (Jolt Physics 5.6 as WASM), https://github.com/jrouwe/JoltPhysics.js, MIT (lib/jolt/LICENSE),
  in games with colliders. Copyright (c) Jorrit Rouwe.
- camera_para.dat, ARToolKit's default camera calibration (from jsartoolkit5's examples).
- The Hiro and Kanji pictures (from AR.js's markers).
- Windows builds: DioramaGame.exe, Diorama's own player, which runs Microsoft Edge WebView2 (the WebView2 runtime is
  part of Windows 11; the loader is from the Microsoft.Web.WebView2 package).
- Windows builds on the C++ runtime: DioramaNative.exe, Diorama's native player (its renderer, the C++ trackers, Dear
  ImGui for the Canvas, QuickJS for the scripts), with SDL2.dll (zlib) and opencv_world4100.dll (OpenCV 4.10, Apache
  License 2.0) beside it.
- Android builds: Diorama's own player app (assets/player/android), built with the Android SDK and Gradle.

Built into Diorama:
- Dear ImGui (MIT), https://github.com/ocornut/imgui
- SDL2 (zlib), https://www.libsdl.org
- cgltf (MIT), https://github.com/jkuhlmann/cgltf
- stb_image, stb_image_write, stb_truetype (MIT / public domain), https://github.com/nothings/stb
- ImGuiColorTextEdit (MIT), https://github.com/BalazsJako/ImGuiColorTextEdit
- OpenCV 4.10 (Apache License 2.0), https://opencv.org: the native trackers (surfaces, ArUco, ARToolKit-style markers,
  calibration), the native player and the tools (optional).
- Jolt Physics 5.6.0 (MIT), https://github.com/jrouwe/JoltPhysics: the editor's Simulate and the native player's physics.
- QuickJS (quickjs-ng 0.10.1, MIT), https://github.com/quickjs-ng/quickjs: the native player's scripts.
- OpenCV's ArUco dictionaries as bits (src/aruco_dicts.h, from OpenCV 4.10, Apache License 2.0).

Ideas and methods:
- The surface tracker follows https://github.com/CursedPrograms/AR-Plane-Detection (CLAHE, ORB, homography).
- Indoor navigation follows "Augmented Reality in Indoor Navigation", IJSREM vol. 07 issue 03 (2023),
  doi:10.55041/IJSREM18172.

The art gallery template (templates/gallery): the pictures and the frame model are from
https://github.com/CursedPrograms/ARToolkit-ArtGallery-Template (Cursed Entertainment).
